# 8. GAMEPLAY SEQUENCE — COMPLETE EXPERIENCE

The game should have one continuous primary objective.

The player must leave the ger and reach the river.

## PHASE 1 — WAKE UP

Approximate duration: 30–45 seconds.

- Black screen.
- Eyes open.
- The player discovers the ger interior.
- The player gets up.
- The player can explore briefly.
- No instructions are displayed unnecessarily.

## PHASE 2 — THE EMPTY GER

Approximate duration: 30–60 seconds.

The player can inspect the interior.

Use small atmospheric details:

- A slightly moving curtain.
- Subtle wood creaking.
- Wind outside.
- Dust in moonlight.
- An old door.

Do not create unnecessary puzzles.

The exit is the natural focus.

## PHASE 3 — OPEN THE DOOR

The player approaches the entrance.

An interaction prompt appears subtly.

The player opens the door.

The exterior becomes visible.

The moonlit landscape must feel enormous.

The river should be visible in the distance.

At first, nothing appears to be moving.

## PHASE 4 — THE DEMON APPEARS

The demon stands far away in the steppe.

It must be visible from the ger entrance.

It is approximately 250–300 meters away, depending on the final terrain layout.

It stands completely motionless.

The player should have time to recognize the silhouette.

The Goolingoo-inspired melody begins very quietly.

After a short delay:

- The demon's head moves slightly.
- The white eyes become noticeable.
- Its body turns toward the player.
- It begins floating forward.

The chase starts.

IMPORTANT:

Do not use an immediate loud jumpscare.

Build fear through recognition and anticipation.

## PHASE 5 — THE CHASE

The player must run toward the river.

The demon continuously pursues the player.

There is no combat.

There is no weapon.

There is no hiding system required.

The player must make progress toward the river.

The environment should remain readable.

The demon must be visible often enough to communicate danger.

However, do not force it to remain directly in the center of the camera.

Allow the player to turn around and see it approaching.

## PHASE 6 — THE RIVER

The river is the only safe boundary.

The player must enter the water and cross to the opposite bank.

The water must have visible movement and realistic moonlight reflections.

The player's movement changes while inside the water.

Add water audio and appropriate camera feedback.

The demon approaches the near bank.

It does not cross the river.

## PHASE 7 — THE ENDING

When the player reaches the opposite bank:

- The player exits the water.
- The demon reaches the opposite riverbank.
- It stops.
- It remains completely motionless.
- It stares at the player through its long black hair.
- The Goolingoo-inspired melody stops.
- All major horror ambience fades into silence.

Allow the player to look at the creature for a few seconds.

Do not immediately cut to black.

The ending should feel uncomfortable and unresolved.

Fade to black.

Display:

YOU SURVIVED.

Then:

ГЭХДЭЭ ТЭР ОДОО Ч ЧАМАЙГ ХАРСААР...

Display the game title:

ГОВИЙН ГАНЦ АЙЛ

