## 11.1 Dynamic distance audio

The melody begins when the demon becomes visible.

Its intensity depends on the distance between the player and the demon.

Far distance:
- Quiet.
- Distant.
- Soft.
- Slightly muffled.

Medium distance:
- More audible.
- Clearer melodic detail.
- Slightly increased volume.

Close distance:
- Stronger.
- More distorted.
- More unsettling.
- Subtle additional layers.

Extremely close:
- Intense.
- Uncomfortable.
- Distorted.
- Strong low-frequency presence.

When the demon stops at the river:
- The melody fades completely.
- The environment becomes silent.

## 11.2 Audio implementation

Use:

- Web Audio API or the project's available audio engine.
- Smooth volume interpolation.
- Distance-based attenuation.
- Low-pass filtering.
- Subtle distortion.
- Layered audio.
- Spatial positioning where appropriate.

Avoid abrupt volume jumps.

The melody must transition smoothly as the distance changes.

Do not restart the audio file every frame.

