# 22. HORROR PACING

The experience should follow a controlled horror curve.

### Beginning: Isolation

Quiet.

Uncomfortable.

Familiar environment.

No immediate monster.

### Discovery: Something is wrong

The empty ger.

The open landscape.

The distant white figure.

The player begins to understand that something is present.

### Recognition: The demon

The demon is visible.

The melody begins.

The player realizes it is looking toward them.

### Panic: Chase

The demon starts moving.

The melody grows louder.

The player runs.

The river becomes the only objective.

### Desperation: Near the river

The demon gets closer.

Breathing becomes heavier.

The music becomes more distorted.

The river sound becomes clearer.

### Relief: Crossing

The player reaches the other bank.

The demon stops.

The melody disappears.

### Final discomfort

The demon continues staring.

The player survives.

But the creature does not disappear.

Silence.

Black screen.

This pacing is more important than adding random jumpscares.

